 a y - a y + 2y\u00b2/\u221a3 = (\u221a3 a\u00b2)/2 - 2a y + 2y\u00b2/\u221a3\n\nTherefore, Volume = 2\u03c0 \u222b\u2080^{(\u221a3 a)/2} [ (\u221a3 a\u00b2)/2 - 2a y + (2y\u00b2)/\u221a3 ] dy\n\nNow, integrate term by term:\n\nFirst term: \u222b (\u221a3 a\u00b2)/2 dy = (\u221a3 a\u00b2)/2 * y\n\nSecond term: \u222b -2a y dy = -2a * (y\u00b2/2) = -a y\u00b2\n\nThird term: \u222b (2y\u00b2)/\u221a3 dy = (2/\u221a3) * (y\u00b3/3) = (2y\u00b3)/(3\u221a3)\n\nEvaluate each from 0 to h = (\u221a3 a)/2.\n\nFirst term evaluated at h: (\u221a3 a\u00b2)/2 * (\u221a3 a)/2 = (\u221a3 * \u221a3 a\u00b2 * a)/4 = (3 a\u00b3)/4\n\nAt 0: 0\n\nSecond term evaluated at h: -a * ( (\u221a3 a)/2 )\u00b2 = -a * (3a\u00b2)/4 = -3a\u00b3/4\n\nThird term evaluated at h: (2/(3\u221a3)) * ( (\u221a3 a)/2 )\u00b3 = (2/(3\u221a3)) * ( (3\u221a3 a\u00b3)/8 ) = (2 * 3\u221a3 a\u00b3)/(3\u221a3 * 8 ) = (6\u221a3 a\u00b3)/(24\u221a3 ) = (6a\u00b3)/24 = a\u00b3/4\n\nPutting all together:\n\nFirst term: 3a\u00b3/4\n\nSecond term: -3a\u00b3/4\n\nThird term: a\u00b3/4\n\nTotal integral result: (3a\u00b3/4) + (-3a\u00b3/4) + (a\u00b3/4) = (0) + (a\u00b3/4) = a\u00b3/4\n\nThen multiply by 2\u03c0:\n\nVolume = 2\u03c0 * (a\u00b3/4) = \u03c0 a\u00b3 / 2\n\nWait, but that seems too straightforward. Let me check the calculation again step by step.\n\nFirst, expanding the product inside the integral:\n\n[ (\u221a3 a)/2 - y ] * [ a - (2y)/\u221a3 ]\n\nMultiply term by term:\n\nFirst term: (\u221a3 a)/2 * a = (\u221a3 a\u00b2)/2\n\nSecond term: (\u221a3 a)/2 * (-2y/\u221a3 ) = (\u221a3 a)/2 * (-2y)/\u221a3 = (-2y a)/2 = -a y\n\nThird term: -y * a = -a y\n\nFourth term: -y * (-2y)/\u221a3 = 2y\u00b2/\u221a3\n\nSo, combining:\n\n(\u221a3 a\u00b2)/2 - a y - a y + 2y\u00b2/\u221a3 = (\u221a3 a\u00b2)/2 - 2a y + 2y\u00b2/\u221a3\n\nYes, that's correct.\n\nNow, integrating term by term from 0 to h = (\u221a3 a)/2.\n\nFirst integral term:\n\n\u222b\u2080^h (\u221a3 a\u00b2)/2 dy = (\u221a3 a\u00b2)/2 * h = (\u221a3 a\